<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#maxBytesPerCall> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Largest byte value, in bytes, a single function call may read, decode or return (hxf:bytes, hxf:decodedBytes, hxf:value, hxf:hel). Default 1048576 (1 MiB). A call that would exceed it yields an unbound result and records the reason for hxf:explain."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#maxBytesPerCall> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#maxCellsPerWindow> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Largest number of array cells one windowed call may visit (hxf:stat over a window or a whole array, hxf:window). Default 1000000. A window above it is refused: hxf:stat is unbound and hxf:window yields no rows."@en .
