<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#rank> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Number of dimensions of the array."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#rank> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#rank> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#reads> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A vocabulary term the function reads from the graph."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#reads> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#reads> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reads"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#row> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Row of the cell containing world point (wx, wy): floor for asref:PixelCorner (default), nearest centre for asref:PixelCenter."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#row> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#row> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Raw sample at column x, row y. The array is the band's araster:hasArray, else the grid's, else the grid struct's single array field. A band is a RasterBand IRI or a one-based index and is applied along dlv:axisBand when the array has one."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAtTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The cell at round(seconds * asig:sampleRate) along dlv:axisTime; the one-based channel is applied along dlv:axisBand."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAtTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAtTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAtWorld> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "sampleAt at (column(t, wx, wy), row(t, wx, wy)) where t is the dataset's asref:hasGeoTransform."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAtWorld> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#sampleAtWorld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#signature> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Argument list and result, in the notation name(arg: type, ...) -> type. A trailing ? marks an optional argument."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#signature> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#signature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "signature"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#stat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "min, max, sum, mean or count over the whole array or a half-open window. Refused above hxf:maxCellsPerWindow."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#stat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#stat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#total> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "True when this function always answers, so an unbound result from it would be a defect rather than a described outcome. Only hxf:explain claims this: it reports what went wrong, and a diagnostic that can itself go missing is of no use at the moment you need it."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#total> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#unboundWhen> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A condition under which this function yields no value rather than a wrong one. Repeatable. Absence does not mean the function is total: the library-wide failure contract still applies."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#unboundWhen> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#value> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The node's parsed scalar, mapped by the profile or not. Unbound for structs, lists and arrays."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#value> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#value> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#window> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Property function enumerating every cell of a half-open window, row-major, binding its indices and value. Refused above hxf:maxCellsPerWindow. NON-PORTABLE: this is an Apache Jena ARQ property function (a magic predicate in a triple pattern), not a SPARQL 1.1 filter function nor a SHACL-AF function, so it runs only on Jena/ARQ with the Hexplain engine registered; other SPARQL processors read it as an ordinary triple pattern that matches nothing."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#window> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#window> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#wkt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A GeoSPARQL WKT literal from a WKB or GeoPackage payload. The CRS is the GeoPackage SRS id, else asref:hasCRS/asref:epsgCode on the node or the nearest ancestor."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#wkt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#wkt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#worldX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "World X of grid position (col, row) under an affine geotransform; a missing skew reads as 0."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#worldX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#worldX> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#worldY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "World Y of grid position (col, row) under an affine geotransform; a missing skew reads as 0."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#worldY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn#worldY> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> .
